ular  franchises  one being pokemon and the other being  spirited away  the pokemon that resembles the crawler's  face is the cubone  and from spirited away it would be no  face since the skull crawler had to  represent a hyper carnivore  that was also a kaiju it was in need of  a fresh facial design  not covered by toho in the past thus  came the skeletal features inspired by  anime  the exoskeleton going down from the head  and face  we come to the body and especially the  upper torso and not surprisingly enough  it also has the skeletal features that  seem to protrude from the skin  and outwards like a pseudo exoskeleton  protecting the creatures  insides for this part of the body the  designs came from the xenomorph of the  alien franchise  the cinema of aliens are the ultimate  life forms and they had some sort of  bony exoskeleton that covered  the entire body especially the ribs and  the shoulders which were also seen in  the skull crawler's designs  as the ribs seemed to protrude out of  the body and even the spine from the  back  and a prehensile tail the jaw so  going back to the head we forgot to  discuss about a very important feature  which is the jaw  although it is a part of the face of the  skull crawler we decide to discuss it  separately  as the monster had the jaws that were  very similar to that of the mosasaurus  and what is the mossosaurus you say it  is an extinct marine reptile that lived  during the time of the dinosaurs and  died out along with them  this creature had a very long and  slender snout and teeth that were  conical and sharp  excellent for grabbing and tearing apart  flesh  these extinct creatures had very  powerful jaw strength as well  with a bite force of 33 000 pounds per  square inch  which was at least as powerful as the  tyrannosaurus rex  the eyes now for the eyes and most  notably  what appears to be the eye sockets of  their skull-like heads  are merely empty openings their real  eyes are set much further back  with the opening or sockets perhaps  serving to distract enemies from their  more vulnerable eyes  and they also act as heat-seeking  sensory pits  a real-life animal that has such an  adaptation is the king of the oceans  a killer whale's eyes are on each side  of its head just behind  and above the corner of its mouth and in  front of its white  eye spot the most popular theory is that  the orca eye spots  protect their actual eyes by providing a  false target  and in the same way the skull crawlers  also evolved to have false eye spots to  distract enemies  the reptilian guilds in the novelization  it is stated that the skull crawlers are  amphibious  as we were mentioned as one in the  boneyard  had gills this is similar to the monster  verse godzilla who is also a reptile  but strangely possesses guilds but the  question arises as to why they never  left the island  and go out hunting somewhere else well  for one these  skull crawlers are hyper carnivorous and  were in a constant state of starvation  and hunting in the open seas would have  taken way too much of their energy  as they might not be so much adapted to  catching fishes and marine life forms  therefore they might have just died in  the open seas  but they did try to reach out to  ghidorah's alpha call  but were killed by kong when they tried  to leave the island  the mimicry the novelization states that  the skullcrawlers can mimic human cries  and that this was the reason and cause  of gunpei ikari's death  as he and marlow mistook one for an  eewee child crying  the book also suggests that the largest  skullcrawlers appeared  when it did because it somehow sensed  that kong was down  and might have understood and heard  certain sounds that were familiar  to when kong's parents cried out in pain  the inspirations  for the skull crawlers adaptation is  taken from the predator this alien can  imitate sounds of humans and use it to  lure them into a trap during a hunt  this feature was also seen in wrath of 